# The pictures of pattern.md: a post (a small circle) and a
# construction line drawn, the post extruded and repeated along the
# line; the number of copies changed; last, the flange example, bolt
# holes round a circle. Coordinates are those of the 600x600 headless
# window.
cursor on
key c
move 200 300
down L 200 300
up L 200 300
move 220 300
down L 220 300
up L 220 300
key esc
key s
move 200 200
down L 200 200
up L 200 200
move 400 200
down L 400 200
up L 400 200
key esc
key esc
# The line made construction (G), so that only the circle is extruded.
move 300 200
down L 300 200
up L 300 200
key g
key esc
shot pattern-1-sketch gw
key x shift
view default
move 300 200
down L 300 200
up L 300 200
shot pattern-2-path gw
menu Features|Pattern Along Path
# Wide enough for the path's name.
size tw 900 600
view rotated
menu View|Zoom To Fit
cursor off
shot pattern-3-patterned
cursor on
twmove 143 125
mark 28 122 160 22 tw
shot pattern-4-copies-link tw
twdown L 143 125
twup L 143 125
edit 5
cursor off
shot pattern-5-five-copies
size tw 600 600
# The flange example, in a new file: bolt holes round a pitch circle.
answer no
menu File|New
file $repo/examples/scripts/flange/flange.go
menu Script|Run File...
view rotated
menu View|Zoom To Fit
shot pattern-6-flange
